                <pb facs="0124" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/700: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-07T21:00:00-04:30">December 7, 1941—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. Department’s circular telegram December 7, 4 p.m. Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs informed and he conveyed the message to President Medina who authorized
                    him to tell me that the United States has the entire sympathy of Venezuela and
                    that the Venezuelan Government is determined to fulfill all of its obligations
                    in defense of the continent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
